1
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:48,965
PERFECT CROWN

2
00:00:54,216 --> 00:00:55,631
SPONSORED BY: MINISTRY OF
CULTURE, SPORTS AND TOURISM

3
00:00:55,712 --> 00:00:57,213
AND KOREA CREATIVE
CONTENT AGENCY

4
00:00:57,536 --> 00:00:59,473
MBC DRAMA SCRIPT
CONTEST WINNER

5
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:00,977
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

6
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,979
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

7
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,356
- When did I ever ask...
- Stop that.

8
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:08,610
You didn't see a doctor
after what happened, did you?

9
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:17,202
Don't you think
I'd be quite the supportive wife?

10
00:01:32,383 --> 00:01:33,384
What are you doing?

11
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:37,680
Stay still.

12
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:13,758
I saw a camera.

13
00:02:15,927 --> 00:02:16,928
Oh.

14
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:23,351
Is it still there?

15
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,613
Should we try that again?

16
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:37,824
I think we can give them a better angle.

17
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:41,452
Maybe like…

18
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:50,545
Now.

19
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:52,380
Come on.

20
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:58,970
PERFECT CROWN

21
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:01,472
{\an8}EPISODE 4

22
00:03:02,473 --> 00:03:04,225
{\an8}Did you see their kiss last night?

23
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:05,935
{\an8}They're totally in love.

24
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:08,354
{\an8}- It kept me up all night.
- So romantic.

25
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,067
{\an8}Let's just go.

26
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,821
{\an8}Announcing Grand Prince I-AN.

27
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:36,174
LOVE ACROSS SOCIAL DIVIDES

28
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,259
LOVE DEFYING SOCIAL CLASS…

29
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:39,928
…I-AN AND SEONG'S MIDNIGHT TRYST

30
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:42,847
We can no longer delay
an official statement.

31
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:45,433
This matter will cause public unrest.

32
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,018
We should be cautious...

33
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:48,645
Staying silent now

34
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,730
would only make things worse.

35
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:54,567
Are you hoping I deny it?

36
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:56,569
Your honor is at stake here.

37
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:57,904
A grand prince…

38
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:02,283
may kiss a woman and then
dismiss it as a mere dalliance?

39
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:05,453
Is this the honor
you wish for me to uphold?

40
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:06,537
That maiden

41
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:10,041
is a mere commoner of illegitimate birth.

42
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:20,635
Make it public.

43
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:31,145
As His Royal Highness stated,
this is a scandal by a grand prince.

44
00:04:31,771 --> 00:04:33,356
We must do damage control.

45
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:34,816
"Damage control"?

46
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,734
With that in mind,

47
00:04:37,735 --> 00:04:38,861
you should confirm it.

48
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,573
However,

49
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:45,785
you must state firmly
that there is no prospect of marriage.

50
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,913
Say that your acquaintance
has only just begun,

51
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:50,456
with no talk of marriage.

52
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:54,377
That should minimize any uncertainty.

53
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,586
Prime Minister Min.

54
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:58,631
There's nothing unusual about a young pair
falling in and out of love.

55
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:00,091
If we treat it lightly,

56
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:02,218
it will remain that way.

57
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:06,723
Let it be so.

58
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:07,807
However…

59
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:12,687
that maiden should move out
of your private residence.

60
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:14,522
- Why?
- Your Royal Highness!

61
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:18,359
Not only was she pelted with eggs
at her own home with private security,

62
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:21,112
but she is also bearing the brunt
of every insult online.

63
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:22,488
As if that were not enough,

64
00:05:23,197 --> 00:05:26,034
she was photographed behind the palace,
under palace security.

65
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:29,162
If anything happens to her
because she was left alone,

66
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:31,414
will you answer for it?

67
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,379
We may end up parting ways,

68
00:05:39,881 --> 00:05:41,758
or she may become my future wife.

69
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:45,303
Your Royal Highness, how could you…

70
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:47,347
My residence is already home to many.

71
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,643
<i>Attendants who maintain the grounds.</i>

72
00:05:54,103 --> 00:05:55,605
<i>The Royal Guard for my safety.</i>

73
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:58,566
<i>And there are even cats
that roam in my garden.</i>

74
00:06:00,234 --> 00:06:02,195
The addition of my lady to that list…

75
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:06,741
will have little effect.

76
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:12,622
Where will Your Royal Highness reside?

77
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:17,627
If Ms. Seong is permitted to stay
at your private residence for her safety,

78
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:20,129
then you must stay at the palace.

79
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,840
If rumors spread
that the palace is divided…

80
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:26,427
over a single woman,

81
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:28,763
it will be a grave matter.

82
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,941
ROYAL SECRETARIAT:
OFFICIAL STATEMENT

83
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:41,692
This was approved?

84
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:44,779
Is this how you chose
to handle the matter?

85
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:49,325
- You must compose yourself.
- How can I?

86
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:54,038
Even if marriage is ruled out,

87
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:57,583
once the palace acknowledges them,
that woman will gain status.

88
00:06:58,292 --> 00:07:00,461
Public interest is already at its peak.

89
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:02,463
Should he dare to include her
in state matters...

90
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:03,798
If you knew as much,

91
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:07,093
you should have exercised restraint.

92
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:12,056
Had you just left it alone,
the matter would've resolved itself.

93
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,975
Criticism was already pouring in.

94
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:17,103
"Failure to uphold the dignity
of his station and proper decorum."

95
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:18,771
They had plenty of grounds.

96
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:20,064
However,

97
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:24,026
because Your Majesty has opposed
the Grand Prince,

98
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:26,988
public opinion has shifted in his favor.

99
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:30,992
In fact, criticism of Your Majesty
has already begun to surface.

100
00:07:34,829 --> 00:07:36,122
Just give your approval.

101
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:41,252
I will take care of the rest.

102
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:44,547
Do you have a plan?

103
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:50,261
There is no shortage of noblemen eager
to become the Prince's father-in-law,

104
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:54,098
and plenty in the business world are eager
to keep that woman in check as well.

105
00:07:57,810 --> 00:07:59,729
That is to say,

106
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:03,107
should something happen,
it would hardly be a surprise.

107
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:10,656
<i>The Royal Secretariat
has just released an official statement.</i>

108
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,367
<i>In a royal first, the palace
has acknowledged a courtship</i>

109
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:15,119
<i>that isn't an engagement or marriage.</i>

110
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:19,040
<i>We'll discuss this with formal royal
spokesman, Professor Hwang Wookyeong.</i>

111
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:21,834
<i>- Welcome.
- Hello, it's nice to meet you.</i>

112
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:24,837
<i>You have always maintained the stance…</i>

113
00:08:24,921 --> 00:08:25,922
Hwang Wookyeong?

114
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:27,632
Don't you know who that is?

115
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:31,177
He used to be a royal spokesman
before he got blacklisted.

116
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:34,013
Come on, you must know him. Last year,

117
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:36,849
he was the one who claimed

118
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:39,852
the late king's death
wasn't an accident, but a murder.

119
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,729
A nut who jumps to conspiracy theories.

120
00:08:41,812 --> 00:08:42,897
Be quiet.

121
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:47,068
<i>Many have noted that
this official statement is unprecedented.</i>

122
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:48,152
<i>What do you think?</i>

123
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:50,988
{\an8}<i>I consider it to be
very befitting of the royal family.</i>

124
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:54,742
<i>Castle Group's Seong Huiju
is a commoner and businesswoman.</i>

125
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:57,703
<i>She is far from a traditional royal bride
by palace standards.</i>

126
00:08:57,787 --> 00:09:00,831
{\an8}<i>But it would've been difficult
for the palace to deny the relationship.</i>

127
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:04,919
{\an8}<i>After all, there were
several definitive eyewitness accounts.</i>

128
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:07,547
<i>So are you suggesting that</i>

129
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,674
<i>they had no choice but to recognize it?</i>

130
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:11,884
<i>- That's correct.
- Then Grand Prince I-AN…</i>

131
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:12,969
Seong Huiju.

132
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:16,013
<i>…and what is the likelihood of marriage?</i>

133
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:17,932
<i>Marriage would be highly unlikely.</i>

134
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:20,768
{\an8}<i>Uh, I doubt the royal family
would accept a commoner,</i>

135
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:24,146
{\an8}<i>given their sensitivity about lineage.</i>

136
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:27,775
<i>Then how do you think
the royal family will proceed?</i>

137
00:09:28,317 --> 00:09:31,779
<i>I don't expect them to provide
any further comments on the matter.</i>

138
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:34,782
THE GRAND PRINCE CLIMBED
OVER A WALL

139
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:36,993
I knew this would happen.

140
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:39,870
I told you we should've tried again.

141
00:09:41,038 --> 00:09:42,415
Well, I just…

142
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:46,043
This angle is totally off. Darn it.

143
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,753
What, are we in elementary school?

144
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:50,172
We look like toddlers smooching.

145
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,133
That's what you care about right now?

146
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:53,884
- We kissed and...
- Your Royal Highness.

147
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:55,720
Marketing only works

148
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:59,724
when it's unbelievably sexy or shameless.

149
00:09:59,807 --> 00:10:00,850
"Courtship"?

150
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:03,853
Wishy-washy words like that
will get us nowhere.

151
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:05,313
A tryst at a hotel!

152
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,273
That's sexy.

153
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:09,150
Prince I-AN's shotgun wedding!

154
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:12,528
That's shameless, right?

155
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:16,157
Doesn't it sound tempting, like junk food?

156
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:43,726
The quicker we get married,
the quicker we get divorced.

157
00:10:43,809 --> 00:10:45,811
Okay?

158
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:55,863
Royal weddings are meant
to be conducted step by step…

159
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:57,782
Do you have that much time to waste?

160
00:10:57,865 --> 00:10:58,991
I don't.

161
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:00,242
I mean…

162
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:03,287
Then what? Should we really make it
a shotgun wedding?

163
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:05,414
- So it's sexy and shameless?
- Yes.

164
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:08,376
When you pursue
a venture everyone opposes,

165
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:12,338
you can't give them time to object.

166
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,256
With that in mind…

167
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:18,052
Are you free now?

168
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:24,308
All of a sudden? Why do you ask?

169
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:31,691
I have a little time.

170
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:35,820
Can I take you somewhere?

171
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:38,739
Let's speed things up a bit.

172
00:11:42,326 --> 00:11:43,327
Speed things up?

173
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:47,998
That's enough.

174
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:51,293
Do I look like a kindergartner to you?

175
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:54,505
Stay still.

176
00:11:54,588 --> 00:11:56,841
Let's show them
what we're made of this time.

177
00:11:56,924 --> 00:12:00,761
Since when do people
show others up with their hair?

178
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:05,599
You were in sweats in those photos
where you were caught sucking face.

179
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,729
They must be roasting His
Royal Highness for having terrible taste.

180
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:11,188
It makes me so upset.

181
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:12,982
What's wrong with his taste?

182
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:16,652
I mean, he chose me.
He clearly has exquisite taste.

183
00:12:16,736 --> 00:12:19,613
And those sweats are super expensive.

184
00:12:19,697 --> 00:12:23,200
Gosh. You must be a bird lover.

185
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:25,828
Just look at that magnificent bird's nest
on your head.

186
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:31,584
- You did that on purpose. You…
- Stay still.

187
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:38,007
You really want me to clear your day?
All of it?

188
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:44,764
I'm just worried for your sake.
It'll make tomorrow brutal for you.

189
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:46,515
And for me too.

190
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,642
She wants to be Princess Diana.
What can I do?

191
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:50,352
Princess Diana?

192
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:53,606
As in Princess Diana from the UK?

193
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:54,690
Jeez.

194
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:58,194
All this fuss will die down with time.

195
00:12:58,277 --> 00:13:01,280
That's what the Queen Mother
is waiting for.

196
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:04,366
I won't let that happen.

197
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:08,120
Your Royal Highness.

198
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:47,284
Ta-da.

199
00:13:47,368 --> 00:13:49,829
Isn't she stunning?
Like an angel come to life.

200
00:13:53,958 --> 00:13:55,501
Sure…

201
00:13:55,584 --> 00:13:57,044
…ly not.

202
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,214
You went for "spoiled princess"
and not an actual princess?

203
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,805
Is he for real?

204
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,686
I told you this wasn't my vibe!

205
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,029
I mean,

206
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:27,241
he's dressed in a princely suit.
What's his problem?

207
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,285
That's what I'm saying, bro.

208
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:30,494
He is beyond difficult.

209
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,710
My goodness.

210
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:01,692
Please give us a moment.

211
00:15:01,775 --> 00:15:03,402
- I shall quickly fix this...
- No need.

212
00:15:29,553 --> 00:15:30,763
Sorry about that.

213
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,660
Thank you so much.

214
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:02,836
Perhaps a bit too plain?

215
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,171
Really?

216
00:16:06,423 --> 00:16:08,092
I see what you mean.

217
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:12,346
He does look a bit dull and old-fashioned.

218
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:16,684
What the…

219
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,353
- What are you doing?
- Seriously?

220
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:20,896
Are you feeling shy or something?

221
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,857
A royal never feels shy… Oh.

222
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,275
Just lose this.

223
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:28,320
Losing the pocket square
makes it a little bit less dull.

224
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:30,114
Better, right?

225
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:33,951
No, I was actually talking
about you, Ms. Seong.

226
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:35,703
Oh.

227
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:36,870
Me?

228
00:16:37,454 --> 00:16:38,622
That's not possible.

229
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:40,457
How could you ever call me plain?

230
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:47,339
I'm dazzling.

231
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:53,595
So pretty.

232
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:17,327
Go, Castle!

233
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:21,749
- Let's go, Sharks!
- Let's go, Sharks!

234
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:24,209
- Come on, Sharks!
- Let's go!

235
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:31,425
It's not too late to call the Royal Guard.

236
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,094
We'd be better without them here.

237
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:38,932
Your Royal Highness!

238
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:40,684
Ooh!

239
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,186
Here we go.

240
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:44,730
Let's see here.

241
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:46,190
CASTLE SHARKS' LUCKY CHARM

242
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:49,401
Ooh, I have such a keen eye for detail.

243
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:50,819
You're 2XL, right?

244
00:17:51,361 --> 00:17:53,238
If we wear matching outfits…

245
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:55,699
- He cannot.
- Why not?

246
00:17:55,783 --> 00:18:00,537
His Royal Highness can't wear uniforms.
No expression of political views.

247
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:02,915
This isn't politics. It's just sports.

248
00:18:02,998 --> 00:18:05,542
"A royal's private life
is never truly private,"

249
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:06,877
is the palace's position.

250
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:13,383
Matching outfits would create some buzz.

251
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:18,305
- Then you can just wear it, Aide Choi.
- Really?

252
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:21,433
- It's so much more fun to cheer in this!
- So excited!

253
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:25,521
Your Royal Highness,
remember I have warm undertones?

254
00:18:25,604 --> 00:18:26,647
This is perfect for me.

255
00:18:27,231 --> 00:18:28,857
You're not wearing this.

256
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,400
Why not?

257
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:43,914
Hey, you!

258
00:18:44,665 --> 00:18:46,708
Why have you been ignoring my calls?

259
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:48,418
Why you little…

260
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:50,546
Oh, His Royal Highness?

261
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:52,840
Your Royal Highness.

262
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:54,800
What brings you to such squalid grounds?

263
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:58,095
Fried chicken?

264
00:18:58,178 --> 00:18:59,638
You're getting ahead of yourself.

265
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:03,016
We don't speak until His Royal Highness
speaks to us first.

266
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,226
Oh!

267
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:06,687
Huiju has told me a lot about you.

268
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:08,272
About me?

269
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:09,356
What?

270
00:19:09,439 --> 00:19:11,942
You better keep your trap shut.

271
00:19:12,651 --> 00:19:14,611
I wonder what she told you.

272
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:17,072
Oh, right.

273
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:19,658
Yes.

274
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:25,122
It is an honor to make your acquaintance,
Your Royal Highness.

275
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:26,915
I am Dayeong of the Han Family.

276
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:28,584
And your father's name?

277
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:31,420
He is Jeongseok of the Han family.

278
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:33,630
Former Minister of Justice.

279
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:36,341
What a commendable father you have.

280
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:42,890
Oh.

281
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:45,976
Jeongwoo's throwing the first pitch?

282
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:47,603
All right. Let's go!

283
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:54,109
It appears we have Prime
Minister Min for the first pitch today.

284
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,194
That's right.

285
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:57,321
He's famous for being
a hardcore fan of the Castle Sharks.

286
00:19:57,404 --> 00:20:01,950
I hear he even dreamed of being
a baseball player when he was young.

287
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:04,369
I'm excited to see
how his first pitch will turn out.

288
00:20:11,668 --> 00:20:14,588
That was
a beautiful pitch. Do you hear that crowd?

289
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:16,757
The crowd is going wild for him.

290
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,842
The crowd's love for Prime Minister Min is

291
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:21,178
through the roof here
at Gocheok Sky Dome today.

292
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:22,429
I couldn't agree more.

293
00:20:24,681 --> 00:20:26,058
Min Jeongwoo!

294
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:35,150
Up to bat is Gang Suho.

295
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,862
He pulled that one. It's high and deep.

296
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:40,113
Is it going over?

297
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,531
Over the wall and gone!

298
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:43,992
Gang Suho pulls off a comeback win!

299
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,786
Home run!

300
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:47,829
Nanny Jung!

301
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:49,498
You okay?

302
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:52,000
<i>The Castle Sharks
are sinking their teeth in…</i>

303
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:53,252
Are you all right?

304
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:57,172
I am fine, Your Majesty.

305
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:00,300
But the treat from Lord INPYEONG is…

306
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:02,511
No need for concern.

307
00:21:06,306 --> 00:21:08,308
The corndog is safe.

308
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:11,353
It certainly is not, Your Majesty!

309
00:21:11,853 --> 00:21:13,563
<i>If we take a look, the stands are packed</i>

310
00:21:13,647 --> 00:21:15,148
<i>with fans in Castle Sharks jerseys…</i>

311
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:19,987
Your Royal Highness.

312
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:22,072
- The Sharks…
- Stop it, babe.

313
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:24,574
Get lost.

314
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:26,702
Let's go, Gang Suho!

315
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:28,829
You got this, Sharks!

316
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:31,623
Your Royal Highness.

317
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:33,208
Jeongwoo.

318
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:36,962
You didn't leave after the first pitch?
I thought you'd already left.

319
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,423
My secretary said
not to waste the photo op.

320
00:21:39,506 --> 00:21:41,091
Photo op?

321
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:51,560
Scooch over, Your Royal Highness.
Jeongwoo needs a seat.

322
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:56,398
Scooch over.

323
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,527
Come sit here, Jeongwoo.

324
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,200
You should have some too.

325
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:09,119
No, thank you.

326
00:22:09,202 --> 00:22:10,203
You're not hungry?

327
00:22:11,288 --> 00:22:12,873
- I am.
- Then eat.

328
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:16,001
Are you a picky eater?

329
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:19,838
- It's not that…
- He can only eat at restaurants.

330
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:21,548
Why?

331
00:22:21,631 --> 00:22:24,092
Because quality and safety
can't be guaranteed elsewhere.

332
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:25,677
And it's quite unseemly.

333
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,514
Am I expected to do that too?

334
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:33,310
- Kiss!
- Kiss!

335
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:36,772
{\an8}- Kiss!
- Kiss!

336
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:40,275
{\an8}On the Kiss Cam,
we have the hottest couple of the moment.

337
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:41,651
- That's right.
- It's them.

338
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:42,736
Oh, my gosh!

339
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:44,571
They really look great together.

340
00:22:44,654 --> 00:22:47,282
But I'm sure it won't be easy
for His Royal Highness to kiss

341
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:48,658
- on the Kiss Cam.
- Right.

342
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:50,660
- Kiss!
- No! Stop!

343
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:53,288
- Kiss!
- No! They can't kiss!

344
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:57,417
- Kiss!
- No kiss! Where's the camera?

345
00:22:57,501 --> 00:23:00,379
- Kiss!
- Kiss!

346
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:03,673
- Kiss!
- No! They can't kiss! No kiss!

347
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:05,217
No kiss!

348
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:09,554
- Kiss!
- Kiss!

349
00:23:09,638 --> 00:23:12,099
- Kiss!
- Kiss!

350
00:23:12,182 --> 00:23:17,479
- Kiss!
- Kiss!

351
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:18,730
{\an8}MUST UPHOLD HIS DECORUM

352
00:23:22,401 --> 00:23:23,402
{\an8}Sorry, we can't.

353
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:24,903
{\an8}No, we can't!

354
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:26,530
{\an8}We can't kiss.

355
00:23:39,084 --> 00:23:40,085
Hold on.

356
00:23:40,669 --> 00:23:43,964
How are we supposed to be photographed
if they're covering us like this?

357
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:47,843
- Huiju, let's go get dinner.
- Yeah?

358
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:49,136
We had corndogs already.

359
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:51,179
That's not enough to fill you up.

360
00:23:51,721 --> 00:23:53,265
Remember what you wanted last time?

361
00:23:54,015 --> 00:23:55,600
- Last time?
- Yeah.

362
00:23:56,518 --> 00:23:59,062
Mmm. Oh, that!

363
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:01,231
Your Royal Highness.

364
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:03,275
Yes?

365
00:24:03,358 --> 00:24:04,359
Back to the palace?

366
00:24:05,318 --> 00:24:07,028
- What?
- Go on without me.

367
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:08,613
I'll have dinner with Jeongwoo.

368
00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:09,990
I shall join you.

369
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:11,700
Pardon?

370
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:15,162
We came here together, so wouldn't it
be odd if we left separately?

371
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:37,726
Bye!

372
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:56,995
Prime Minister Min.

373
00:24:57,662 --> 00:24:58,830
Yes, Your Royal Highness.

374
00:25:00,499 --> 00:25:01,791
Slow day at the office?

375
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:04,544
Pardon?

376
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:17,557
Mmm, it looks so good.

377
00:25:18,808 --> 00:25:19,893
Please eat up.

378
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:27,275
We can't eat before you take a bite.
Please, go ahead.

379
00:25:28,485 --> 00:25:30,195
You should've gone back to the palace.

380
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:33,114
Hmm? What now? Is there another issue?

381
00:25:33,615 --> 00:25:35,367
This is a restaurant, isn't it?

382
00:25:35,909 --> 00:25:36,993
I know.

383
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:38,870
A royal shall never consume raw food.

384
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:39,955
It's the law.

385
00:25:41,122 --> 00:25:43,917
Shall we order some gyeran-jjim
or doenjang soup for you?

386
00:25:44,501 --> 00:25:45,710
- No need.
- Wait, hold on.

387
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:47,879
So, raw food? Nothing raw?

388
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:50,715
Not even beef tartare?
You can't have anything like that?

389
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:52,968
I cannot.
The risk of food poisoning is too high.

390
00:25:54,636 --> 00:25:55,762
What a load of crap.

391
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:57,556
Load of…

392
00:25:59,766 --> 00:26:02,477
- A load of crap…
- You can't have street food.

393
00:26:02,561 --> 00:26:04,062
Nothing raw either.

394
00:26:04,145 --> 00:26:06,439
Where are you supposed
to find the joy in life?

395
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:09,484
That's why you shouldn't marry
His Royal Highness.

396
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:10,652
Too many restrictions.

397
00:26:11,945 --> 00:26:14,281
What else? What else can't you do?

398
00:26:25,834 --> 00:26:27,252
Here I am.

399
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:31,840
Should we do this puzzle?

400
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:35,135
Hwan, may I try on your Dragon Robe?

401
00:26:35,218 --> 00:26:36,219
Sure.

402
00:26:41,099 --> 00:26:42,100
Let's see here.

403
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:45,937
Whoa, you look great in it.

404
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:48,481
- It looks good on me, right?
- Yeah.

405
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:52,652
Father, Hwan said I could…

406
00:26:56,406 --> 00:26:58,116
How dare you mock

407
00:26:58,700 --> 00:27:01,161
the Crown Prince's authority!

408
00:27:13,590 --> 00:27:15,842
<i>Do not wear red.</i>

409
00:27:15,925 --> 00:27:17,260
<i>That is the king's color.</i>

410
00:27:18,219 --> 00:27:19,554
<i>Do not walk ahead.</i>

411
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:22,682
<i>The king always leads.</i>

412
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:27,896
<i>Do not question anything.</i>

413
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:31,316
<i>It is the king's command.</i>

414
00:27:58,426 --> 00:27:59,719
Eat up while you still can.

415
00:28:00,970 --> 00:28:04,140
You won't be able to
after the royal wedding.

416
00:28:15,652 --> 00:28:18,446
Mmm, so good. It's delicious.

417
00:28:21,116 --> 00:28:22,325
Your Royal Highness.

418
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:24,160
Were you at a raw fish restaurant?

419
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:27,205
- Do not worry. I did not eat any.
- And a baseball stadium?

420
00:28:27,288 --> 00:28:28,790
Do not worry about that either.

421
00:28:28,873 --> 00:28:30,125
No personal show of support.

422
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:31,459
No security issues.

423
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:33,253
It was unannounced, so no reporters.

424
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:35,755
You should have maintained decorum.

425
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:37,173
I did.

426
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:40,009
What is the use if you maintain it,
when she will not?

427
00:28:40,093 --> 00:28:41,803
Because she has no reason to.

428
00:28:42,679 --> 00:28:44,639
She is not a member
of the royal family yet.

429
00:28:45,807 --> 00:28:50,061
Do you truly not see that her faults
will soon become your own?

430
00:28:51,896 --> 00:28:54,357
What on earth were you doing
while this unfolded?

431
00:28:58,528 --> 00:28:59,821
We have no other choice.

432
00:29:00,321 --> 00:29:01,573
I shall step in.

433
00:29:02,490 --> 00:29:03,491
And do what?

434
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:06,995
Your Royal Highness cannot be
expected to know a woman's proprieties,

435
00:29:07,078 --> 00:29:10,707
and it would be improper
for the Queen Mother to step forward.

436
00:29:11,374 --> 00:29:12,917
That leaves only me, does it not?

437
00:29:13,668 --> 00:29:17,297
I… am afraid I do not understand.

438
00:29:17,380 --> 00:29:18,381
Please allow me

439
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:21,176
to discipline her.

440
00:29:27,557 --> 00:29:30,059
Even palace attendants
who run wild like colts

441
00:29:30,143 --> 00:29:31,478
become well-behaved

442
00:29:32,061 --> 00:29:33,730
after I am done with them.

443
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:36,024
Rest assured, Your Royal Highness.

444
00:29:39,819 --> 00:29:40,820
Goodness me.

445
00:29:42,947 --> 00:29:45,116
Such excellent news. I am so relieved.

446
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,827
I have full faith in you.

447
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:49,788
Such excellent news indeed.

448
00:29:56,628 --> 00:29:59,506
Gosh, are you leaving already?
You need to have breakfast.

449
00:29:59,589 --> 00:30:01,424
It's okay. I normally skip breakfast.

450
00:30:01,508 --> 00:30:03,092
That simply will not do. Eat up.

451
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:05,595
Special apple bunnies for you. Open up.

452
00:30:06,346 --> 00:30:07,472
There's some fuzz here.

453
00:30:08,056 --> 00:30:09,307
- It's okay.
- Open up.

454
00:30:12,685 --> 00:30:14,521
We can skip all this next time...

455
00:30:14,604 --> 00:30:16,356
- Have a lovely day.
- Have a lovely day.

456
00:30:51,724 --> 00:30:53,643
Oh, right. We met at the palace last time.

457
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:55,770
I am Jinsook of the Choi Family.

458
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:58,106
Feel free to address me
as Court Lady Choi.

459
00:30:58,690 --> 00:30:59,816
Court Lady Choi.

460
00:31:00,525 --> 00:31:01,776
Where are my manners?

461
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:05,989
I am Seong Huiju.

462
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:08,950
I am the head court lady
of Anhwadang Hall,

463
00:31:09,033 --> 00:31:10,535
the residence of the Grand Prince…

464
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:18,334
Hey, Ms. Do.

465
00:31:20,128 --> 00:31:22,964
Of course, I'm on my way.

466
00:31:24,883 --> 00:31:26,551
Yes, I swear I'm on my way.

467
00:31:27,051 --> 00:31:29,804
I can see Umyeonsan Tunnel up ahead.

468
00:31:32,265 --> 00:31:33,808
I'm almost there.

469
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:35,643
I see you, Ms. Do.

470
00:31:36,144 --> 00:31:37,437
I'm not lying!

471
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:39,606
So?

472
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:41,858
You just got in the car and left?

473
00:31:41,941 --> 00:31:44,235
Yes. Was it something urgent?

474
00:31:45,862 --> 00:31:47,906
Court Lady Choi must be irritated.

475
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:50,742
<i>Why?</i>

476
00:31:53,953 --> 00:31:56,623
She has been biding her time to teach you.

477
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:00,251
What exactly would she teach me?

478
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:04,172
The overall protocols, history,
and hierarchy of the royal family.

479
00:32:04,255 --> 00:32:05,465
Things like that.

480
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:15,058
Good morning, Ms…

481
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:17,810
That sounds like a waste of time.

482
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:20,980
<i>Fine. I'll take the lessons.</i>

483
00:32:21,522 --> 00:32:23,107
<i>I need to go. Bye.</i>

484
00:32:29,864 --> 00:32:30,865
Wow.

485
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:35,703
Are you sure
you two weren't close in school?

486
00:32:38,206 --> 00:32:39,540
What? Why?

487
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:41,209
It's just that

488
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,586
you two make such a cute couple.

489
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:53,972
Cute couple, my foot.

490
00:32:56,808 --> 00:32:59,227
What? There's a lot to do today.

491
00:32:59,852 --> 00:33:01,312
You have a lot of meetings too.

492
00:33:01,396 --> 00:33:02,939
You couldn't trim it down a bit?

493
00:33:03,022 --> 00:33:04,816
I did. I trimmed a lot.

494
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:08,152
Fine, let's hear it. Keep it very brief.

495
00:33:08,236 --> 00:33:12,031
First off, you have a new product testing
with the R&D manager in one hour.

496
00:33:12,115 --> 00:33:13,574
You have one hour to do that.

497
00:33:13,658 --> 00:33:14,659
One hour?

498
00:33:15,159 --> 00:33:16,786
- For a new product testing?
- Yes.

499
00:33:17,286 --> 00:33:20,331
You have lunch with Gang Taehyun
from Castle Pharma at 1:00.

500
00:33:22,041 --> 00:33:23,710
Why would he have lunch with me?

501
00:33:23,793 --> 00:33:25,003
Isn't he in Taeju's circle?

502
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:26,713
He joined yours as of yesterday.

503
00:33:26,796 --> 00:33:29,048
All of a sudden?

504
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:30,717
Didn't you also kiss the Grand Prince

505
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:32,552
all of a sudden?

506
00:33:40,101 --> 00:33:41,144
Was he good?

507
00:33:41,227 --> 00:33:42,228
What?

508
00:33:42,311 --> 00:33:45,273
I mean, the cheeks were flushed.
Totally blushing for real.

509
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:46,357
Hey, come on.

510
00:33:47,150 --> 00:33:49,819
I was really hot that night.

511
00:33:49,902 --> 00:33:51,863
That outfit is surprisingly warm.

512
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:54,949
Not you.

513
00:33:55,616 --> 00:33:56,784
His Royal Highness.

514
00:33:57,618 --> 00:33:58,703
What?

515
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:01,039
Did you get all fluttery too?

516
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:04,751
Listen, Ms. Do.

517
00:34:05,251 --> 00:34:06,753
Do I look like a teenager to you?

518
00:34:06,836 --> 00:34:10,923
Why would I blush and get all fluttery
over a measly kiss?

519
00:34:11,007 --> 00:34:12,050
Don't make me laugh.

520
00:34:12,133 --> 00:34:14,552
I see. Not so great, huh?

521
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:17,055
Then again, he has no dating experience.

522
00:34:19,182 --> 00:34:21,893
He has no dating experience?

523
00:34:21,976 --> 00:34:22,977
Really?

524
00:34:23,561 --> 00:34:26,147
He's never publicly dated anyone.
No tabloid rumors either.

525
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:28,816
That's what you meant?

526
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:30,985
You may be wrong about that.

527
00:34:32,612 --> 00:34:34,197
I guess he was surprisingly good.

528
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,907
Yeah, he clearly knew his way around…

529
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:39,077
Hey. That's not what I meant!

530
00:34:41,204 --> 00:34:43,206
I'm not sure what you meant, but I got it.

531
00:34:43,289 --> 00:34:44,957
Shall we get going now?

532
00:34:45,041 --> 00:34:46,375
Why? What now?

533
00:34:46,459 --> 00:34:48,795
We'll barely have enough time
for the tailor as it is.

534
00:34:48,878 --> 00:34:50,254
New clothes?

535
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:51,339
For what?

536
00:34:52,006 --> 00:34:53,007
Prime Minister Min did?

537
00:34:53,091 --> 00:34:54,342
That's what I'm telling you.

538
00:34:54,842 --> 00:34:55,885
It hasn't…

539
00:34:56,928 --> 00:34:58,763
Could we have some privacy?

540
00:34:58,846 --> 00:35:00,056
Yes, sir.

541
00:35:05,478 --> 00:35:07,480
It hasn't been made public yet,

542
00:35:07,563 --> 00:35:10,483
but the PR team said
he invited Huiju to the roundtable.

543
00:35:10,566 --> 00:35:12,610
But even Father was never invited to that.

544
00:35:12,693 --> 00:35:15,404
Exactly! He threw money
and sucked up to them for an invite,

545
00:35:15,488 --> 00:35:18,324
but they treated him like dirt
because he wasn't a noble.

546
00:35:19,534 --> 00:35:21,994
Why would they invite Seong Huiju?

547
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:25,748
Babe, what would you hate more?
Huiju moving up in society

548
00:35:25,832 --> 00:35:27,667
or becoming the heir to Castle Group?

549
00:35:28,459 --> 00:35:29,544
I hate both equally.

550
00:35:29,627 --> 00:35:32,213
But still, out of the two,
wouldn't the former be better?

551
00:35:32,296 --> 00:35:36,384
Do you really want to see me bow down
and address her as Your Highness?

552
00:35:36,467 --> 00:35:39,137
Babe, you need to step back
and see the bigger picture.

553
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:42,515
She doesn't become "Her Highness"
just because she marries him.

554
00:35:43,057 --> 00:35:45,268
We may have to bow down a bit…

555
00:35:46,435 --> 00:35:48,146
- Hey, Han Dayeong. I...
- But!

556
00:35:48,729 --> 00:35:50,022
She can't run a business.

557
00:35:50,106 --> 00:35:52,650
Royals aren't allowed
to engage in economic activities.

558
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:55,444
No, I still don't like it.

559
00:35:55,528 --> 00:35:58,030
What if she divorces him
after she becomes "Her Highness"?

560
00:35:58,906 --> 00:36:00,158
Babe.

561
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:01,993
Have you ever heard of a royal divorce?

562
00:36:04,162 --> 00:36:05,454
I thought they could.

563
00:36:05,538 --> 00:36:06,622
If that were true,

564
00:36:06,706 --> 00:36:09,458
Grand Prince I-AN
should've ascended the throne.

565
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:11,586
Wouldn't that have made more sense?

566
00:36:13,004 --> 00:36:14,005
Maybe you're right.

567
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:17,800
- Babe, we should get a gift for Huiju.
- What?

568
00:36:17,884 --> 00:36:20,553
We'll back her up
and get her married off to the Crown

569
00:36:20,636 --> 00:36:22,722
so you can claim
Castle Group all for yourself.

570
00:36:26,475 --> 00:36:28,519
I don't know.

571
00:36:31,147 --> 00:36:32,148
Come on now.

572
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:35,151
Who does Taeju belong to?

573
00:36:35,818 --> 00:36:36,819
To Dayeong.

574
00:36:38,029 --> 00:36:39,947
Who does Castle Group belong to?

575
00:36:43,117 --> 00:36:44,118
To me.

576
00:37:04,013 --> 00:37:05,473
You stopped driving it around?

577
00:37:06,557 --> 00:37:08,768
- What?
- The red open-top car.

578
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:13,606
Did the Prince tell you to stop?

579
00:37:14,941 --> 00:37:16,901
As if I would ever listen.

580
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:19,570
It's in the shop.

581
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:21,489
They have a pick-up
and drop-off service now.

582
00:37:22,365 --> 00:37:23,491
It broke down?

583
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:25,451
But you just got that car.

584
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:28,454
Yeah. Someone hit the bumper and ran.

585
00:37:28,537 --> 00:37:29,538
Who?

586
00:37:29,622 --> 00:37:30,957
How would I know?

587
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:33,251
But then again,

588
00:37:34,126 --> 00:37:36,629
there are a lot of people
who'd like to crash my car.

589
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:49,392
I'm back.

590
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:52,687
Her Ladyship is here.

591
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:54,939
- Let me help you.
- Your Ladyship!

592
00:37:55,022 --> 00:37:56,816
- I'll take that.
- No, I can carry them.

593
00:37:56,899 --> 00:37:58,067
Just let me.

594
00:37:58,150 --> 00:38:00,528
- Did you go shopping?
- Yeah. I can put those away.

595
00:38:00,611 --> 00:38:01,779
Did you have dinner?

596
00:38:02,655 --> 00:38:04,031
I had a light salad.

597
00:38:04,115 --> 00:38:05,491
Get Her Ladyship dinner first.

598
00:38:05,574 --> 00:38:06,742
- No, it's okay.
- Sure.

599
00:38:06,826 --> 00:38:09,370
- We made sujeonggwa earlier...
- You are late.

600
00:38:25,469 --> 00:38:26,721
I know it is late,

601
00:38:27,346 --> 00:38:29,557
but your royal education
cannot be delayed.

602
00:38:30,641 --> 00:38:32,018
I ask for your understanding.

603
00:38:33,769 --> 00:38:35,563
Yes, of course.

604
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:38,232
I understand.
I understand indeed.

605
00:38:40,026 --> 00:38:41,819
Do not repeat yourself.

606
00:38:41,902 --> 00:38:43,362
It makes you look frivolous.

607
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:45,489
Okay.

608
00:38:46,657 --> 00:38:48,534
Dragging out the ends of your words

609
00:38:49,201 --> 00:38:50,286
is also forbidden.

610
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:52,872
Yep.

611
00:38:53,748 --> 00:38:56,876
Your education will be comprehensive.

612
00:38:56,959 --> 00:39:01,422
For your public role, you will learn
royal protocol, royal history,

613
00:39:01,505 --> 00:39:04,342
proper conduct, and the court hierarchy.

614
00:39:04,842 --> 00:39:05,843
For your private role,

615
00:39:05,926 --> 00:39:08,763
you will learn who to meet
and whom to avoid.

616
00:39:08,846 --> 00:39:10,264
What to say…

617
00:39:11,974 --> 00:39:14,602
and what not to say.

618
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:16,896
Let us start with your posture.

619
00:39:27,281 --> 00:39:29,075
Your standing posture

620
00:39:30,326 --> 00:39:31,452
is good.

621
00:39:32,745 --> 00:39:33,746
Please walk.

622
00:39:34,497 --> 00:39:35,498
Up to there.

623
00:39:43,214 --> 00:39:44,423
More energy.

624
00:39:56,811 --> 00:39:57,853
Stand up straight.

625
00:40:01,982 --> 00:40:04,568
Can you not even stand still?

626
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:19,417
Though you are small in stature,

627
00:40:19,917 --> 00:40:21,419
do not bow your head.

628
00:40:22,503 --> 00:40:24,422
Posture is dignity.

629
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:26,090
Do you understand?

630
00:40:27,091 --> 00:40:29,552
Yes, Queen Mother.

631
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:36,142
No, that is not right.

632
00:40:37,935 --> 00:40:39,645
Let me show you one last time.

633
00:40:39,728 --> 00:40:41,021
Watch carefully.

634
00:40:44,233 --> 00:40:46,402
Like this.

635
00:40:46,485 --> 00:40:49,196
Extend your leg.

636
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:50,406
Extend…

637
00:40:50,990 --> 00:40:52,199
Oh, dear.

638
00:40:54,076 --> 00:40:55,369
Right here.

639
00:40:55,453 --> 00:40:57,913
- It hurts right here, doesn't it?
- Yes, it does.

640
00:40:57,997 --> 00:40:59,957
You have so many knots here.

641
00:41:00,541 --> 00:41:02,460
This must hurt a lot.

642
00:41:02,543 --> 00:41:04,003
- Yes, a bit.
- Here too.

643
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:06,255
- Does this hurt even more?
- That is right.

644
00:41:06,338 --> 00:41:08,257
Oh, my goodness.

645
00:41:09,133 --> 00:41:12,136
I've been doing Pilates for ten years,

646
00:41:12,219 --> 00:41:14,722
so I can just tell from someone's posture.

647
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:19,143
- Now is not the time for this…
- No, now is exactly the right time.

648
00:41:19,226 --> 00:41:20,853
Let's try that once more.

649
00:41:20,936 --> 00:41:22,521
- All right.
- I'll help you.

650
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:25,691
- Like this?
- There you go. Lift your leg and…

651
00:41:25,774 --> 00:41:27,109
Good.

652
00:41:27,193 --> 00:41:28,527
You said to leave it to you.

653
00:41:29,278 --> 00:41:30,738
Is this how you discipline?

654
00:41:31,405 --> 00:41:32,615
Your Royal Highness!

655
00:41:57,431 --> 00:41:58,432
Hey.

656
00:41:59,308 --> 00:42:00,643
We have a lot of eyes on us.

657
00:42:01,727 --> 00:42:03,562
Please take her away.

658
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:05,856
What?

659
00:42:06,774 --> 00:42:08,734
Do you know how much work I have to do?

660
00:42:08,817 --> 00:42:11,862
Must I devote my whole night
to posture correction?

661
00:42:14,573 --> 00:42:16,116
Your Royal Highness.

662
00:42:21,455 --> 00:42:23,749
What brings you to your private residence?

663
00:42:24,959 --> 00:42:26,877
I have been away from it for far too long.

664
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:30,589
And I was curious to see
how your royal lessons were progressing.

665
00:42:30,673 --> 00:42:32,007
Please make your return.

666
00:42:32,091 --> 00:42:33,634
The palace gates will soon be shut.

667
00:42:41,225 --> 00:42:42,893
- You should come with me.
- Pardon?

668
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:45,229
Your primary duty
is to protect Anhwadang Hall,

669
00:42:45,813 --> 00:42:47,356
not discipline her. Is that not so?

670
00:42:47,856 --> 00:42:49,942
- But Your Royal Highness...
- Do not argue.

671
00:42:50,025 --> 00:42:51,110
It is my command.

672
00:43:15,593 --> 00:43:17,219
With the Ancestral Rite concluded,

673
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:19,680
we will begin planning the overseas tour.

674
00:43:26,145 --> 00:43:27,354
How many stops this year?

675
00:43:29,732 --> 00:43:31,358
It should be similar to last year.

676
00:43:36,071 --> 00:43:38,198
Why? Shall I reduce them?

677
00:43:38,782 --> 00:43:39,950
Won't you stop me?

678
00:43:42,077 --> 00:43:43,329
- What?
- My marriage.

679
00:43:44,538 --> 00:43:46,040
I thought you'd try at least once.

680
00:43:48,626 --> 00:43:49,668
I am not you.

681
00:44:02,473 --> 00:44:04,808
You may be able to decide something

682
00:44:04,892 --> 00:44:07,811
simply based on whether you find
something agreeable or not.

683
00:44:09,229 --> 00:44:10,564
But if I do that…

684
00:44:21,450 --> 00:44:22,910
the country would collapse.

685
00:44:23,494 --> 00:44:24,912
Checkmate.

686
00:44:28,457 --> 00:44:29,875
I'd rather you yelled at me.

687
00:44:36,256 --> 00:44:37,841
I handled the Junghwajeon incident.

688
00:44:40,344 --> 00:44:43,180
The Queen Mother should no longer
take issue with it either.

689
00:44:51,438 --> 00:44:53,190
In a royal funeral,

690
00:44:54,024 --> 00:44:57,986
the body is cleansed and an ablution
is performed at the Place of Passing,

691
00:44:58,696 --> 00:45:01,740
along with the ritual wailing,
the fencing, mouth-filling,

692
00:45:01,824 --> 00:45:03,826
and ice-bedding ceremonies.

693
00:45:03,909 --> 00:45:06,954
- The Royal Ancestral Altar...
- They really do all that?

694
00:45:08,163 --> 00:45:11,333
It is discourteous to interrupt.

695
00:45:11,917 --> 00:45:14,294
My apologies. I was just really curious.

696
00:45:14,920 --> 00:45:17,506
Did they do all that three years ago too?

697
00:45:18,173 --> 00:45:19,341
That is correct.

698
00:45:20,175 --> 00:45:21,593
Why don't I remember it at all?

699
00:45:23,095 --> 00:45:26,390
The last public funeral ceremony
held by the royal family

700
00:45:26,932 --> 00:45:28,726
was in 2005.

701
00:45:29,435 --> 00:45:30,436
Why?

702
00:45:32,688 --> 00:45:36,024
<i>The mother of the Grand Prince,
Queen UIHYEON,</i>

703
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:38,902
<i>passed away 20 years ago,</i>

704
00:45:38,986 --> 00:45:41,572
<i>in the fourth lunar month
of the Eulyu year.</i>

705
00:45:48,036 --> 00:45:52,124
<i>His father, King HUIJONG,
passed away seven years later,</i>

706
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:55,794
<i>in the sixth month of the Imjin year.</i>

707
00:46:06,722 --> 00:46:08,557
<i>And just three years ago,</i>

708
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:10,559
<i>His Majesty's father</i>

709
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:15,314
<i>and Grand Prince I-AN's older brother,
King SEONJONG, passed away.</i>

710
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:23,363
<i>With tragedies so frequent,</i>

711
00:46:23,989 --> 00:46:26,533
<i>the royal family decided
to keep the ceremony private.</i>

712
00:46:30,245 --> 00:46:31,246
Your Ladyship?

713
00:46:31,330 --> 00:46:32,790
It's just all too much.

714
00:46:32,873 --> 00:46:34,958
- Pardon?
- It's no wonder

715
00:46:35,584 --> 00:46:38,086
His Royal Highness
has a chip on his shoulder.

716
00:46:38,587 --> 00:46:40,297
I mean, I knew all about it,

717
00:46:41,673 --> 00:46:43,592
but to hear about it one after the other…

718
00:46:48,222 --> 00:46:49,348
Don't mind me.

719
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:52,976
I just want to be alone right now.

720
00:47:05,614 --> 00:47:06,949
QUEEN UIHYEON PASSED AWAY…

721
00:47:07,032 --> 00:47:08,325
"Queen UIHYEON

722
00:47:09,034 --> 00:47:11,245
passed away
in a vehicle rollover accident."

723
00:47:13,622 --> 00:47:14,665
KING HUIJONG PASSED…

724
00:47:14,748 --> 00:47:17,125
"King HUIJONG passed away
after a heart attack."

725
00:47:18,001 --> 00:47:19,878
"Could it have been prevented?"

726
00:47:23,966 --> 00:47:27,845
"King SEONJONG
tragically met his death in a fire."

727
00:47:38,105 --> 00:47:39,690
And if he suffers indigestion?

728
00:47:39,773 --> 00:47:41,066
You would be wholly to blame.

729
00:47:41,149 --> 00:47:42,776
And if Queen Mother is angered?

730
00:47:44,403 --> 00:47:46,530
Is that why he was so on edge back then?

731
00:47:55,372 --> 00:47:57,666
PRINCE

732
00:48:09,469 --> 00:48:10,512
Is he working?

733
00:48:19,605 --> 00:48:20,814
Please introduce yourself.

734
00:48:21,690 --> 00:48:24,359
She has been
my closest companion recently.

735
00:48:27,029 --> 00:48:29,031
I am Jaegyeong of the Kim Family,

736
00:48:29,531 --> 00:48:30,866
Your Royal Highness.

737
00:48:31,867 --> 00:48:35,537
There is a dinner
with the royal correspondents tomorrow.

738
00:48:36,705 --> 00:48:39,625
I cannot accompany you due to my illness.

739
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:40,876
Take her in my stead.

740
00:48:42,002 --> 00:48:44,212
Her father is
the proprietor of Jeongui Daily.

741
00:48:44,796 --> 00:48:46,381
She will be able to aid you.

742
00:48:50,510 --> 00:48:53,764
You have been falling ill
quite frequently lately.

743
00:48:53,847 --> 00:48:56,433
Perhaps because I have had
a lot on my mind.

744
00:48:59,019 --> 00:49:00,187
Court Lady Im, approach.

745
00:49:02,773 --> 00:49:04,274
What is Her Majesty's ailment?

746
00:49:04,858 --> 00:49:05,859
Pardon?

747
00:49:06,818 --> 00:49:08,236
She has been ill for a few days.

748
00:49:08,862 --> 00:49:10,948
The royal physician must have visited.

749
00:49:11,031 --> 00:49:13,075
What is Her Majesty's ailment?

750
00:49:18,538 --> 00:49:20,165
You have failed in your duties.

751
00:49:20,707 --> 00:49:22,125
Not at all, Your Royal Highness.

752
00:49:24,419 --> 00:49:26,296
Instruct the royal physician

753
00:49:26,380 --> 00:49:29,383
to monitor Her Majesty's condition
three times a day.

754
00:49:29,967 --> 00:49:33,637
The illness may spread,
so private audiences must be forbidden.

755
00:49:34,304 --> 00:49:35,639
That includes Lord INPYEONG…

756
00:49:38,100 --> 00:49:39,726
and most certainly, His Majesty.

757
00:49:48,485 --> 00:49:50,362
You are unwell,
so you should get some rest.

758
00:49:50,946 --> 00:49:53,740
I shall attend the engagement alone.

759
00:49:59,788 --> 00:50:01,373
I feel terrible.

760
00:50:01,456 --> 00:50:04,042
It appears I have upset
His Royal Highness.

761
00:50:05,085 --> 00:50:06,211
Do not be troubled.

762
00:50:07,879 --> 00:50:09,840
Hunting inherently requires

763
00:50:11,008 --> 00:50:12,676
patience above all.

764
00:50:34,031 --> 00:50:35,782
That woman by the Queen Mother's side.

765
00:50:36,450 --> 00:50:38,702
Conduct a comprehensive
background check on her.

766
00:50:38,785 --> 00:50:39,786
Yes, sir.

767
00:50:40,579 --> 00:50:41,580
No.

768
00:50:43,123 --> 00:50:44,374
Start with Jeongui Daily.

769
00:50:44,458 --> 00:50:45,792
Look into them first.

770
00:50:45,876 --> 00:50:47,335
Understood, sir.

771
00:50:51,631 --> 00:50:52,632
Your Royal Highness.

772
00:50:53,175 --> 00:50:55,260
You have a missed call from Ms. Seong.

773
00:50:55,343 --> 00:50:56,344
Several, actually.

774
00:51:09,316 --> 00:51:11,485
THREE MISSED CALLS
JUNIOR ALUM

775
00:51:22,537 --> 00:51:23,538
Your Royal Highness.

776
00:51:23,622 --> 00:51:25,457
<i>What do you need? I'm busy.</i>

777
00:51:25,957 --> 00:51:27,876
Uh, I'm also really…

778
00:51:33,673 --> 00:51:34,966
Let's not get angry.

779
00:51:35,550 --> 00:51:37,844
You must take pity on this poor soul.

780
00:51:41,515 --> 00:51:42,516
Your Royal Highness.

781
00:51:43,100 --> 00:51:45,477
<i>I'm only going to say this once,
so listen carefully.</i>

782
00:51:46,853 --> 00:51:48,021
I'm on your side.

783
00:51:52,984 --> 00:51:57,322
What I mean is, I can only succeed
if you succeed as well.

784
00:51:57,989 --> 00:52:00,700
Husband and wife stand as one, right?

785
00:52:01,451 --> 00:52:04,996
<i>I'm not saying this
because I adore you or anything,</i>

786
00:52:05,080 --> 00:52:06,373
<i>so don't get too excited.</i>

787
00:52:09,918 --> 00:52:11,128
Are you still there?

788
00:52:12,045 --> 00:52:13,171
Hello?

789
00:52:14,840 --> 00:52:15,882
Your Royal Highness?

790
00:52:17,634 --> 00:52:18,635
Did he hang up?

791
00:52:19,177 --> 00:52:20,220
Oh, he did.

792
00:52:21,930 --> 00:52:22,931
Cool.

793
00:52:28,353 --> 00:52:30,355
JUNIOR ALUM

794
00:52:43,160 --> 00:52:44,911
- Choi Hyeon.
- Yes, Your Royal Highness?

795
00:52:48,498 --> 00:52:50,041
I made sure to run over.

796
00:52:50,125 --> 00:52:51,585
Did someone ask you to?

797
00:52:52,752 --> 00:52:53,879
Pardon?

798
00:52:53,962 --> 00:52:55,755
I will head to my private residence
in the evening.

799
00:52:56,590 --> 00:53:00,010
Uh, but Prime Minister Min
requested you stay in the palace…

800
00:53:00,802 --> 00:53:04,931
But where did he come up
with such nonsense?

801
00:53:05,682 --> 00:53:07,267
I shall prepare accordingly.

802
00:53:20,405 --> 00:53:22,574
- To the internet café!
- Remember last time…

803
00:53:26,077 --> 00:53:27,621
Your Majesty!

804
00:53:28,622 --> 00:53:30,790
- Are you all right, Your Majesty?
- Yeah.

805
00:53:31,291 --> 00:53:32,834
Behave yourself before His Majesty!

806
00:53:33,543 --> 00:53:35,003
My apologies, Your Majesty.

807
00:53:42,594 --> 00:53:43,845
You should be more careful.

808
00:53:43,929 --> 00:53:46,014
Yes, Your Majesty. Please get back safely.

809
00:53:47,265 --> 00:53:48,475
- Hey.
- Wait for me.

810
00:53:49,684 --> 00:53:50,727
This way, Your Majesty.

811
00:53:56,900 --> 00:53:59,402
What are you doing here,
Prime Minister Min?

812
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:02,197
Today is not Sunday.

813
00:54:03,698 --> 00:54:04,950
I am aware, Your Majesty.

814
00:54:05,450 --> 00:54:08,328
Unfortunately, I must deal
with an urgent matter this weekend.

815
00:54:08,411 --> 00:54:11,790
I am afraid I must cancel
this Sunday's history lesson.

816
00:54:11,873 --> 00:54:13,833
Official duties must take priority.

817
00:54:13,917 --> 00:54:14,918
Instead,

818
00:54:15,585 --> 00:54:16,836
we will have a lesson today.

819
00:54:17,671 --> 00:54:20,674
Or we could just skip it.

820
00:54:26,471 --> 00:54:27,514
Come this way!

821
00:54:37,983 --> 00:54:39,484
I wish I could play.

822
00:54:49,619 --> 00:54:50,662
Prime Minister Min.

823
00:54:51,871 --> 00:54:52,872
Yes, Your Majesty?

824
00:54:53,456 --> 00:54:55,208
I would like to make a request.

825
00:54:59,671 --> 00:55:03,675
One, two, three, four.

826
00:55:03,758 --> 00:55:06,845
Five, six, seven.

827
00:55:06,928 --> 00:55:08,847
We keep a smile on our face.

828
00:55:08,930 --> 00:55:11,224
Smile. With elegance.

829
00:55:11,308 --> 00:55:12,350
There you go.

830
00:55:12,434 --> 00:55:15,103
One, two, three…
Straighten your back!

831
00:55:17,105 --> 00:55:19,024
- Again!
- Again. Go.

832
00:55:26,323 --> 00:55:30,827
We once again steady our breathing,
while maintaining a smile on our face.

833
00:55:31,328 --> 00:55:34,247
One, two, three, four.

834
00:55:34,331 --> 00:55:39,294
- Five, six, seven, eight.
- At this rate, she'll break all the china.

835
00:55:39,377 --> 00:55:41,838
I know, right? They're not cheap, either.

836
00:55:42,339 --> 00:55:44,507
But does that even help?

837
00:55:45,008 --> 00:55:46,760
I've seen it in period dramas before.

838
00:55:46,843 --> 00:55:48,970
- Put your arms down.
- I doubt it.

839
00:55:49,054 --> 00:55:50,388
Smile!

840
00:55:51,306 --> 00:55:52,432
Smile!

841
00:55:52,515 --> 00:55:54,225
There you go, with elegance.

842
00:55:55,018 --> 00:55:57,479
Six, seven, eight!

843
00:55:57,562 --> 00:56:00,690
One, two, three, four.

844
00:56:00,774 --> 00:56:03,735
Five, six, seven, eight.

845
00:56:03,818 --> 00:56:05,153
- Your Majesty!
- There...

846
00:56:06,112 --> 00:56:07,155
Hello, Your Maje…

847
00:56:16,331 --> 00:56:17,415
So you're saying

848
00:56:18,041 --> 00:56:19,542
you basically played hooky?

849
00:56:19,626 --> 00:56:20,794
How dare you!

850
00:56:20,877 --> 00:56:23,588
I am here to see Uncle.

851
00:56:24,089 --> 00:56:25,799
Did you make an appointment?

852
00:56:27,384 --> 00:56:30,845
Well… No, I did not.

853
00:56:30,929 --> 00:56:32,305
Exactly.

854
00:56:32,389 --> 00:56:35,016
You showed up
without even making an appointment.

855
00:56:35,100 --> 00:56:36,601
To play with your uncle.

856
00:56:37,227 --> 00:56:38,770
That's what playing hooky is.

857
00:56:42,941 --> 00:56:43,942
Well done.

858
00:56:45,026 --> 00:56:46,319
You only live once.

859
00:56:46,403 --> 00:56:48,113
You should play hooky at least once.

860
00:56:49,155 --> 00:56:50,323
Shall we?

861
00:56:57,956 --> 00:56:59,124
What do you want to do?

862
00:56:59,999 --> 00:57:03,169
He has been a bit overwhelmed recently.

863
00:57:04,212 --> 00:57:05,839
He's still young.

864
00:57:07,132 --> 00:57:09,426
If only there were
an age limit for being king.

865
00:57:10,385 --> 00:57:11,386
It's too bad.

866
00:57:13,847 --> 00:57:15,306
Yes…

867
00:57:18,726 --> 00:57:19,727
Sorry.

868
00:57:20,228 --> 00:57:22,730
My husband just wouldn't let me go.

869
00:57:22,814 --> 00:57:26,276
Hmm. You two dated for years,
and you still like each other?

870
00:57:26,359 --> 00:57:28,736
Of course. I like him more every day.

871
00:57:28,820 --> 00:57:30,488
He gets more handsome every day.

872
00:57:30,572 --> 00:57:32,490
And he treats me
better and better every day.

873
00:57:34,576 --> 00:57:37,787
As you should.
You abandoned your family to marry him.

874
00:57:38,580 --> 00:57:39,622
What?

875
00:57:40,665 --> 00:57:44,711
I mean, everyone knows you made
your father collapse when you got married.

876
00:57:44,794 --> 00:57:47,922
He threatened to disown you
and ban you from using the Han name.

877
00:57:48,423 --> 00:57:49,424
It caused quite a stir.

878
00:57:49,507 --> 00:57:50,758
Stop that.

879
00:57:50,842 --> 00:57:53,011
Nobody talks like that anymore.

880
00:57:53,094 --> 00:57:54,387
Oh, please.

881
00:57:54,471 --> 00:57:57,807
Everyone still judges people by status
and pedigree behind closed doors.

882
00:57:57,891 --> 00:57:59,225
We're just jealous.

883
00:57:59,726 --> 00:58:02,312
People like us would never dream of
marrying for love.

884
00:58:04,355 --> 00:58:06,733
I guess you have no idea
what's happening in the world

885
00:58:06,816 --> 00:58:09,068
because you're always cooped up
in your chambers.

886
00:58:09,152 --> 00:58:11,779
My sister-in-law, with her lowly pedigree,

887
00:58:11,863 --> 00:58:13,823
is dating the Grand Prince.

888
00:58:14,449 --> 00:58:15,700
Haven't you heard?

889
00:58:22,499 --> 00:58:23,708
What's wrong?

890
00:58:23,791 --> 00:58:24,918
That witch!

891
00:58:25,793 --> 00:58:28,046
Kim Jaegyeong was like that in school too.

892
00:58:28,129 --> 00:58:29,714
She's just so nasty.

893
00:58:29,797 --> 00:58:32,467
Maybe I should've just dragged her
out of there by her hair.

894
00:58:33,343 --> 00:58:34,928
You should have.

895
00:58:35,011 --> 00:58:36,638
What? Can I do that?

896
00:58:37,597 --> 00:58:38,932
Why not?

897
00:58:39,015 --> 00:58:41,976
Make sure you grab it next time.
I'll cover the settlement.

898
00:58:43,269 --> 00:58:45,021
My sweet husband.

899
00:58:45,563 --> 00:58:48,608
Of course. Money comes before dignity.

900
00:58:48,691 --> 00:58:50,109
This is why you make money.

901
00:58:54,489 --> 00:58:57,075
Here I go.

902
00:58:57,575 --> 00:58:58,618
Done.

903
00:58:59,661 --> 00:59:00,745
Good.

904
00:59:01,538 --> 00:59:02,539
All right.

905
00:59:05,959 --> 00:59:07,001
Now…

906
00:59:09,712 --> 00:59:12,173
you get three chances to hit this pebble.

907
00:59:12,257 --> 00:59:13,883
One, two, three.

908
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:15,843
If it lands inside this circle,

909
00:59:15,927 --> 00:59:17,720
all this land becomes Your Majesty's.

910
00:59:17,804 --> 00:59:19,556
- Easy, right?
- It is.

911
00:59:22,600 --> 00:59:23,601
Jeongwoo!

912
00:59:28,189 --> 00:59:30,817
Min Jeongwoo!

913
00:59:35,697 --> 00:59:36,823
Yes? What do you need?

914
00:59:36,906 --> 00:59:38,157
Jeongwoo…

915
00:59:40,118 --> 00:59:42,996
Prime Minister Min,
you will be the referee.

916
00:59:43,621 --> 00:59:44,622
Me?

917
00:59:44,706 --> 00:59:46,708
The loser has to grant the winner's wish.

918
00:59:46,791 --> 00:59:49,127
Rock, paper, scissors.

919
00:59:49,210 --> 00:59:50,378
I won.

920
00:59:51,129 --> 00:59:52,130
Here we go.

921
00:59:52,213 --> 00:59:53,548
That's one.

922
01:00:09,439 --> 01:00:10,982
Got you!

923
01:00:11,065 --> 01:00:12,400
- I got someone!
- My goodness!

924
01:00:17,363 --> 01:00:21,492
Green light… Red light.

925
01:00:22,160 --> 01:00:23,578
Youngseon, you moved.

926
01:00:24,078 --> 01:00:26,706
Green light…

927
01:00:30,209 --> 01:00:32,879
One, two, three.

928
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:35,798
- Four, five, six, seven.
- Five, six, seven.

929
01:00:35,882 --> 01:00:37,091
- One, two.
- One, two.

930
01:00:37,175 --> 01:00:40,345
- Four!
- Four, five!

931
01:00:40,887 --> 01:00:41,971
One, two!

932
01:00:44,557 --> 01:00:45,892
Well done, Your Majesty!

933
01:00:58,154 --> 01:00:59,322
Wow!

934
01:00:59,405 --> 01:01:00,865
I won!

935
01:01:02,950 --> 01:01:04,952
I said I won!

936
01:01:11,751 --> 01:01:13,002
You did not forget, right?

937
01:01:14,754 --> 01:01:15,755
What?

938
01:01:15,838 --> 01:01:18,299
You promised to grant me a wish.

939
01:01:19,300 --> 01:01:20,301
I said that?

940
01:01:22,011 --> 01:01:24,639
Are you a man of virtue or of profit?

941
01:01:30,144 --> 01:01:31,229
I remember.

942
01:01:37,694 --> 01:01:39,445
This is your wish?

943
01:01:40,029 --> 01:01:41,447
I saw it when I arrived.

944
01:01:42,156 --> 01:01:44,575
I have always wanted
to ride one with the wings.

945
01:01:45,368 --> 01:01:46,744
You cannot, Your Majesty.

946
01:01:46,828 --> 01:01:49,330
It is not an approved vehicle.

947
01:01:49,414 --> 01:01:53,292
But it is a car with wings!

948
01:01:53,376 --> 01:01:57,130
It's the only one in the country!

949
01:01:57,213 --> 01:01:59,048
Observing protocol is a matter of customs.

950
01:01:59,132 --> 01:02:02,260
It is the duty of a man of virtue
to uphold propriety and decorum.

951
01:02:02,343 --> 01:02:03,678
Have you forgotten?

952
01:02:16,274 --> 01:02:19,610
Why are you all saying
I cannot do anything? Why?

953
01:02:20,403 --> 01:02:22,822
I am the king!

954
01:02:22,905 --> 01:02:25,908
- I should be able to do what I want!
- My goodness, Your Majesty.

955
01:02:25,992 --> 01:02:26,993
<i>What did you just say?</i>

956
01:02:27,702 --> 01:02:30,955
His Majesty is at your private residence
with Prime Minister Min.

957
01:02:32,165 --> 01:02:33,291
What's he doing there?

958
01:02:33,374 --> 01:02:35,793
How would I know?

959
01:02:38,087 --> 01:02:41,299
You will be back
before the palace gates are shut, right?

960
01:02:42,633 --> 01:02:45,720
Be sure to keep your eyes on the road.
Don't forget your seat belt.

961
01:02:47,597 --> 01:02:49,056
Call me later, sir!

962
01:03:01,569 --> 01:03:03,905
You must keep
the windows closed at all times.

963
01:03:03,988 --> 01:03:06,115
Yes, I'll be sure to keep them closed.

964
01:03:08,951 --> 01:03:10,119
Must you be the driver?

965
01:03:12,288 --> 01:03:14,791
It's the only one in the country.

966
01:03:14,874 --> 01:03:18,169
I don't want anyone else driving it.

967
01:03:20,671 --> 01:03:23,758
I will be in the escort vehicle
ahead of you and clear the road.

968
01:03:23,841 --> 01:03:25,760
You must not go above 60 km per hour.

969
01:03:25,843 --> 01:03:27,929
And you must stay on the phone with me.

970
01:03:28,471 --> 01:03:29,680
If, by any chance,

971
01:03:30,556 --> 01:03:32,725
an unexpected situation arises…

972
01:03:33,309 --> 01:03:34,644
Don't worry.

973
01:03:35,228 --> 01:03:38,356
I will put His Majesty's safety
above all else.

974
01:03:45,863 --> 01:03:48,324
- And the rear security detail?
- Have them follow me.

975
01:03:48,407 --> 01:03:50,743
I will follow behind Ms. Seong's car.

976
01:03:50,827 --> 01:03:52,411
You will?

977
01:03:52,995 --> 01:03:56,707
If security details surround her car,
people will assume it's a motorcade.

978
01:03:56,791 --> 01:03:58,376
It might attract spectators.

979
01:03:58,459 --> 01:04:00,169
If they discover His Majesty inside...

980
01:04:00,253 --> 01:04:01,587
No, that cannot happen!

981
01:04:03,798 --> 01:04:05,299
May I borrow a car?

982
01:04:05,383 --> 01:04:06,801
Something discreet.

983
01:04:31,409 --> 01:04:32,618
<i>Are there any issues?</i>

984
01:04:32,702 --> 01:04:34,704
No, we're fine.

985
01:04:34,787 --> 01:04:36,873
We're going too slow. That's the issue.

986
01:04:36,956 --> 01:04:38,958
Can we not go any faster?

987
01:04:50,553 --> 01:04:53,306
Let's go!

988
01:04:57,810 --> 01:04:59,186
What's wrong with this?

989
01:05:07,028 --> 01:05:08,154
Your Majesty!

990
01:05:09,196 --> 01:05:10,197
Damn it.

991
01:05:16,913 --> 01:05:18,581
Your Majesty.

992
01:05:18,664 --> 01:05:20,625
You have your seat belt on, right?

993
01:05:35,056 --> 01:05:36,682
Seong Huiju, what's wrong?

994
01:05:37,767 --> 01:05:38,893
Jeongwoo!

995
01:05:39,477 --> 01:05:41,646
The brakes aren't working!

996
01:05:49,236 --> 01:05:51,238
Your Majesty, close your window.

997
01:06:43,499 --> 01:06:44,500
YANGSEO-GYO BRIDGE

998
01:07:08,899 --> 01:07:10,693
Hang on tight, Your Majesty.

999
01:09:03,764 --> 01:09:06,684
PERFECT CROWN

1000
01:09:43,304 --> 01:09:44,763
You even hurt your face?

1001
01:09:44,847 --> 01:09:46,640
When that's all you have going for you?

1002
01:09:46,724 --> 01:09:48,267
<i>Someone messed with your car.</i>

1003
01:09:48,934 --> 01:09:49,977
<i>Let's reconsider this.</i>

1004
01:09:50,060 --> 01:09:51,228
This marriage.

1005
01:09:51,312 --> 01:09:54,481
<i>There has been nothing but trouble
since Prince I-AN entered your life.</i>

1006
01:09:55,065 --> 01:09:56,358
Let's call off this marriage.

1007
01:09:59,361 --> 01:10:00,946
What the hell are you doing?

1008
01:10:01,530 --> 01:10:02,948
{\an8}<i>This is how you protect someone.</i>

1009
01:10:04,158 --> 01:10:06,035
{\an8}Just marry me instead.

1010
01:10:06,118 --> 01:10:08,037
{\an8}Are you trying to protect that maiden?

1011
01:10:08,120 --> 01:10:09,121
{\an8}SAY IT TO MY FACE

1012
01:10:09,205 --> 01:10:10,623
{\an8}You never learned to bend.

1013
01:10:10,706 --> 01:10:12,166
{\an8}Do not bend to their will.

1014
01:10:12,249 --> 01:10:15,085
{\an8}<i>Do not back away and do not compromise.</i>

1015
01:10:16,670 --> 01:10:18,297
{\an8}<i>That's how you and I both</i>

1016
01:10:18,380 --> 01:10:19,798
{\an8}<i>get what we want.</i>

1017
01:10:25,971 --> 01:10:27,348
{\an8}EPILOGUE

1018
01:10:27,431 --> 01:10:29,934
{\an8}- Kiss!
- No! Stop!

1019
01:10:30,017 --> 01:10:32,478
{\an8}- Kiss!
- No! They can't kiss!

1020
01:10:32,561 --> 01:10:35,064
{\an8}- Kiss!
- No kiss! Where's the camera?

1021
01:10:35,147 --> 01:10:36,440
{\an8}Should we speed things up?

1022
01:10:38,025 --> 01:10:39,068
{\an8}Be sexy

1023
01:10:40,152 --> 01:10:41,237
{\an8}and shameless?

1024
01:10:43,948 --> 01:10:49,370
{\an8}- Kiss!
- Kiss!

1025
01:10:49,453 --> 01:10:55,918
{\an8}- Kiss!
- Kiss!

1026
01:10:56,001 --> 01:11:02,216
{\an8}MUST UPHOLD HIS DECORUM

1027
01:11:02,299 --> 01:11:03,342
{\an8}Sorry, we can't.

1028
01:11:03,884 --> 01:11:05,094
{\an8}We can't!

1029
01:11:05,177 --> 01:11:06,470
{\an8}We can't kiss.

1030
01:11:44,425 --> 01:11:46,427
{\an8}Translated by Justin S. Kim

1031
01:11:56,603 --> 01:12:01,442
PERFECT CROWN
